A||||13||Fieroboy1||3.4 Swap question||||1||
Z||000000||Fieroboy1||10-26-2000||08:51 PM||||Hello all.  Just a quick question. I am considering purchasing a junkyard 3.4 camaro motor and dropping it into my 86 GT.  Most of the old 2.8 components are just plain shot and I would rather just install the 3.4 as is from the camaro.  How much trouble will this cause?  Being a longitudinal motor and not transverse originally, is the rotation correct?  Thanks in advance,<P>John McCormick||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-26-2000||09:41 PM||||It won't be as easy as you expect.  I think you need to research this swap a lot more.  I'm having a 3.4 put into my 88 GT.  But I'm paying to have it done. Starter needs repositioning, axles need replacing, water pump modifications.  Small stuff like that.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||10-26-2000||10:28 PM||||Lar, why do the axles need replaced. This is the first I've heard of that.<P>The rotation is the same, but the starter is on the wrong side. I think you just about have to use the Fiero accessories.<P>Check out this link for info.<BR> <A HREF="http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/parks/e-conv.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/parks/e-conv.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||10-27-2000||01:42 AM||||starter needs to be repositioned to the other side and all components from the 2.8 from the heads up go on the 3.4 - the stock 3.4 parts will not work<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                          <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT<BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||10-27-2000||12:36 PM||||BB your right, I'm getting a different transmission with my 3.4 so need different length axles.||||reg||4
Z||000005||88formula||10-27-2000||06:33 PM||||You would probably spend less money replacing your old worn 2.8-liter parts than retrofitting the Camaros system to work.||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||10-27-2000||07:45 PM||||Ah, that explains it, Lar. Are you swapping in a 4 speed auto? If that's the case, I've heard you use the inner axle shafts that fit the tranny and the outer shafts that fit the Fiero and join them at a CV joint. Or am I completely off and out in left field? Anyway, that would explain why you're changing axles.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Old Lar||10-27-2000||10:33 PM||||I'm having Twin Lakes Fiero do the work.  I neither have the skill or patience for the rebuild work. No place to do that work either.  Bob has done many of these swaps before.  A new 3.4 and new T440 auto plus other stuff.  It will be a new car when its done. Not quite as expensive as buying a new Fiero in 1988, but getting close.||||reg||1
Z||000008||BAM-BAM||10-27-2000||11:02 PM||||  Maybe you would consider this as a less expensive option?<P> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=477707703" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=477707703</A> <P>  I haven't heard conclusively that it's a bad deal.<P> Later, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Guages And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||12
Z||000009||Fieroboy1||10-28-2000||09:36 PM||||Thanks for the info guys....Just means i'll have to spend a little more time and sort through my pile of 2.8 parts and do a lot of cleaning.  Just brought home the engine today. 95 camaro motor with 47k on it.  Got most of the engine stripped down of it's camaro parts and already got the fiero intake on.  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||1FieroGTRacingInc||10-28-2000||10:28 PM||||Sound's like fun....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000011||Seanh||10-28-2000||10:45 PM||||I am thinking of doing the 3.4 swap this winter and was wondering. I have read all about what to do to engine to make it work, but, I am hearing of different types of 3.4's from different car and years. I would like one under 60K miles. What year cars and types of engine should I be looking for? I heard you cant use the twin cam engine, is that correct? Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000012||batboy||10-28-2000||11:55 PM||||Well, a couple of the guys have the dual twin cam 3.4 swaps, but I believe it's significantly harder and more expensive to do.||||reg||1
Z||000013||86SE||10-29-2000||07:13 PM||||The engines that are the easiest to put in are the 93-95 Camaro/Firebird pushrod 3.4's.<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||1
